00:57:13.210 --> 00:57:17.080
And that is something
that we are testing out

00:57:17.080 --> 00:57:21.650
with a small set of
customers right now.

00:57:21.650 --> 00:57:23.835
But v6 support for
everything else

00:57:23.835 --> 00:57:25.710
is basically something
that we're working on.

00:57:25.710 --> 00:57:27.582
So stay tuned.

00:57:27.582 --> 00:57:28.534
AUDIENCE: Thank you.

00:57:32.350 --> 00:57:34.580
AUDIENCE: Yes, sorry, the
usual question after IP v6

00:57:34.580 --> 00:57:35.860
is multicast.

00:57:35.860 --> 00:57:37.930
So IP v4.

00:57:37.930 --> 00:57:43.260
Any multicast routing
that you're doing or not?

00:57:43.260 --> 00:57:45.070
INES ENVID: Yeah,
great question as well.

00:57:45.070 --> 00:57:46.320
We got all the hard questions.

00:57:46.320 --> 00:57:47.320
AUDIENCE: Actually, for
enterprise, especially.

00:57:47.320 --> 00:57:48.330
INES ENVID: Yeah.

00:57:48.330 --> 00:57:53.040
No, there's no doubt that a lot
of the enterprise applications

00:57:53.040 --> 00:57:55.695
are running on multicast.

00:57:55.695 --> 00:57:58.760
Actually, we've
been looking at it.

00:57:58.760 --> 00:58:04.020
And multicast is a very
complex capability,

00:58:04.020 --> 00:58:09.720
meaning that it
can be very simple

00:58:09.720 --> 00:58:12.250
or it can be super complex.

00:58:12.250 --> 00:58:14.190
And I think a lot of
different applications

00:58:14.190 --> 00:58:15.880
require different
capabilities there.

00:58:15.880 --> 00:58:19.440
So in order to build
some of those multicasts

00:58:19.440 --> 00:58:23.110
is not negligible task.

00:58:23.110 --> 00:58:25.740
And it could be a little
bit of a rat hole.

00:58:25.740 --> 00:58:27.540
So we've been looking at that.

00:58:27.540 --> 00:58:30.900
We don't have
currently plans that I

00:58:30.900 --> 00:58:34.080
can communicate for that today.

00:58:34.080 --> 00:58:36.170
So that's where we're standing.

00:58:36.170 --> 00:58:40.470
We're watching and see
whether that's something

00:58:40.470 --> 00:58:42.950
that we can't live without or
we really need to implement.

00:58:42.950 --> 00:58:45.227
And we're definitely
open for feedback.

00:58:45.227 --> 00:58:46.560
But that's where we're standing.

00:58:51.092 --> 00:58:53.300
NEHA PATTAN: I think that's
a great set of questions.

00:58:53.300 --> 00:58:56.060
And thanks, everyone,
for attending the talk.

00:58:56.060 --> 00:58:59.560
And thank you, also,
for the questions.

